description:
Fun Country Soaring is the premier soaring club of Northern Ohio. We are located only 50 minutes West of Cleveland and 30 min East of Sandusky / Cedar Point, and the views of Lake Erie from 3,000 feet are breathtaking. 

Operating out of Ortner Airport (I-64) in Wakeman, Ohio, we have access to both a 3,500’ paved runway and a grass strip. FCS has four Flight Instructors and seven Tow Pilots and one of the best fleets that can be found in the mid-west.  Our fleet includes:

  Piper Pawnee tow plane; 
  Blanik l-23 two seat glider; 
  Grob 103 two seat glider; 
  Grob 102 single seat glider; 
  Schweizer 1-26 single seat glider


FCS operates Wednesdays, Saturdays and Sundays, weather permitting and offers scenic flights, glider instruction and glider ratings for power pilots. Visit our web site and Facebook page for more information.

We are always open to new members.  Visit our website:  www.funcountrysoaring.com and our Facebook page:  https://www.facebook.com/groups/funcountrysoaring/ for more information.

Upper Valley Flying Club is a non-profit flying club that operates year-round at the Lebanon, New Hampshire Municipal Airport (KLEB), a Class D towered airport with two 5000+ foot runways. We operate three aircraft.

// 2000 CESSNA 172R (Dual NAV/COM • Dual G5s • GARMIN 430W Navigator  • ADSB In/Out)
// 2002 CESSNA 172S (Dual NAV/COM • Dual G5s •  Garmin 650 Navigator • KAP 140 Autopilot • ADSB In/Out)
// 1978 CESSNA 182RG (Dual NAV/COM • Aspen Pro 1000 • ADSB In/Out • Autopilot • Backup NAV2 CDI)

We allow training in both aircraft with club-authorized instructors.

We meet once a month on third Thursdays, either at our hangars in summer months or at a local restaurant winter months. Meetings are open to the public.
